Inkscape Web license
====================

Inkscape Web is a port of Inkscape (https://inkscape.org) to the web. Most of
its code is derived from Inkscape source code, which is available under the
GNU General Public License, version 2 or later. Inkscape Web source code is
therefore also available under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or
later (GPL-2.0-or-later), unless a file states otherwise.

Ported code keeps the copyright of the original Inkscape authors. See the
header of each file, the upstream file it names in its "Upstream:" line, and
https://gitlab.com/inkscape/inkscape/-/blob/master/AUTHORS.

Notable exceptions:
- packages/wasm compiles upstream Inkscape C++ and third-party libraries with
  their own licenses. See packages/wasm/THIRD-PARTY.md.
- packages/assets copies runtime data (icons, palettes, translations, ...) from
  upstream Inkscape. The built output contains the upstream COPYING, AUTHORS
  and LICENSES files.

The built application links the GNU Scientific Library (GPL-3.0-or-later). As
such, the complete built application is covered by the terms of the GNU GPL
version 3 or later, as are the binaries of upstream Inkscape.

License of individual source files
==================================

The license of each source file is in its first lines after
"SPDX-License-Identifier:". The text of each license is in LICENSES/.
See https://spdx.org/licenses/ for the identifiers.
